      }
    },
    "Two, as in %@'s own terminal. /compact summarises the conversation now, to make room in its context window. /review asks what to review — your changes against a base branch, your uncommitted changes, a commit, or instructions of your own — then %@ reviews it, and the review appears between two notices. Type either alone in the message box. Each runs as a turn of %@'s own, with no message of yours; while a turn runs, it waits above the message box like any message. /compact needs a session with something to summarise, and /review isn't offered in Chat only, because a review reads your files. Any other command is sent to %@ as an ordinary message." : {
      "comment" : "FAQ answer: Codex's /compact and /review in SipAI; placeholder is the Codex label, four times",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有两个，和 %1$@ 自己的终端里一样。/compact 会立即总结对话，为上下文窗口腾出空间。/review 会先问你要审查什么——对照某个基准分支的更改、未提交的更改、某个提交，或你自己写的说明——然后由 %2$@ 进行审查，审查结果显示在两条提示之间。在输入框中单独输入其中一个即可。每个命令都作为 %3$@ 自己的一个回合运行，不带你的消息；如果有回合正在进行，它会像其他消息一样停在输入框上方等待。/compact 需要会话里已有可总结的内容；“仅对话”中不提供 /review，因为审查要读取你的文件。其他任何命令都会作为普通消息发送给 %4$@。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Type instructions and press Enter" : {
      "comment" : "Review picker text field placeholder, in Codex's own words",
