    "Xiaomi" : {
      "comment" : "Provider name; Chinese uses the company's own name",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "小米"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Yes" : {
      "comment" : "Option of a yes-or-no field on an MCP server's form",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "是"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Yes — click the T icon beside the search icon in the toolbar. It appears when at least one of your agent tools is signed in to a plan (a Claude subscription, a ChatGPT plan for %@, or a Kimi Code membership), and it shows what each plan reports: the current 5-hour session and weekly windows for %@, the weekly and per-model limits for %@, and the 5-hour and monthly limits for %@, plus a weekly one on older plans. The numbers are fetched when you open the window and are as fresh as the time shown at the bottom; click the refresh arrow for a new reading. Each figure comes from the tool's own account query, run on your Mac by the tool itself: %@ answers its /usage command, %@ answers over its app server, and %@ answers over its local server. No tokens are spent. Learn more, beside the window's title, opens Settings → Usage, which shows more of what each tool reports — %@'s own account of what is using your limits, %@'s credits, limit resets and token history — and links to each tool's own usage page. A free %@ limit reset is used from there, once you confirm it; it cannot be undone. If every agent runs on an API key there is nothing to show and the icon stays hidden; Settings → Usage says where each one is billed instead." : {
      "comment" : "FAQ answer: plan consumption; placeholders are the Codex, Claude Code and Kimi Code labels",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可以——点击工具栏中搜索图标旁边的 T 图标。当至少一个智能体工具登录了套餐（Claude 订阅、%@ 的 ChatGPT 套餐或 Kimi Code 会员）时它就会出现，并显示各套餐报告的内容：%@ 当前的 5 小时会话窗口和每周窗口，%@ 的每周额度和各模型限额，以及 %@ 的 5 小时和每月限额，较早的套餐还有每周限额。数字在你打开窗口时获取，新鲜程度以底部显示的时间为准；点击刷新箭头可重新读取。每个数字都来自该工具自身的账户查询，由该工具在你的 Mac 上自行运行：%@ 回答它的 /usage 命令，%@ 通过它的 app server 回答，%@ 通过它的本地服务器回答。不消耗任何 token。窗口标题旁的“了解更多”会打开“设置 → 用量”，那里显示各工具报告的更多内容——%@ 自己关于哪些用量占用了你限额的说明，%@ 的点数、额度重置和 token 记录——并链接到各工具自己的用量页面。%@ 的免费额度重置可在那里使用，需要你先确认；使用后无法撤销。如果所有智能体都使用 API 密钥，则没有可显示的内容，图标会保持隐藏；“设置 → 用量”会改为说明每个智能体在哪里计费。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Yes, and allow this host for this conversation" : {
      "comment" : "Codex approval card answer for a network request: allow the host until the turn ends, in codex's own words",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "是，并在此对话中允许此主机"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Yes, and bypass permissions" : {
      "comment" : "Plan card button: approve the plan and carry on with every permission check bypassed, as the turn was before it planned",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "是，并跳过权限确认"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Yes, and don't ask again for these files" : {
      "comment" : "Codex approval card answer: allow edits to these files until the turn ends, in codex's own words",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "是，且对这些文件不再询问"
          }
        }
